---
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import Sidebar from "../components/Sidebar.astro";
---

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>Beginner Guide - Motto Immortal</title>
</head>
<body>
  <Sidebar />

  <!-- HERO SECTION -->
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-overlay"></div>
    <div class="hero-text">
      <span class="hero-tag">New Player</span>
      <h1 class="hero-headline">Beginner Guide</h1>
      <p class="hero-sub">Everything you need to know to start strong in Motto Immortal</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- MAIN CONTENT -->
  <main class="main-content">

    <!-- TABLE OF CONTENTS -->
    <div class="content-card toc-card">
      <h2>📋 What's in This Guide</h2>
      <div class="toc-grid">
        <a href="#early-heroes" class="toc-item">
          <span class="toc-icon">⚔️</span>
          <span>Best Early Game Heroes</span>
        </a>
        <a href="#relics" class="toc-item">
          <span class="toc-icon">🔮</span>
          <span>Relic Priority</span>
        </a>
        <a href="#zodiac" class="toc-item">
          <span class="toc-icon">♈</span>
          <span>Zodiac Selection</span>
        </a>
        <a href="#pvp-normal" class="toc-item">
          <span class="toc-icon">🏆</span>
          <span>Normal Arena Teams</span>
        </a>
        <a href="#pvp-triple" class="toc-item">
          <span class="toc-icon">⚡</span>
          <span>Triple Duel (Advanced)</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- SECTION 1: EARLY HEROES -->
    <div class="content-card" id="early-heroes">
      <h2>⚔️ Best Early Game Heroes — and Why</h2>
      <p>
        In Motto Immortal, your first investment decisions define your entire progression path. 
        Spreading resources too thin will stall you. Focus on these heroes first.
      </p>

      <h3>🥇 Top Priority Heroes</h3>

      <div class="hero-entry">
        <h4>Fangi <span class="tier-badge sss">Early Meta Pick</span></h4>
        <p>
          Fangi is one of the most efficient early investments in the game. A Divine Fangi with a 
          Level 30 relic can dominate PvP and performs well across nearly all game modes. 
          Build this hero early and you will maintain a strong position throughout your progression.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="hero-entry">
        <h4>Poseidon <span class="tier-badge s">S-Tier Tank</span></h4>
        <p>
          Poseidon is a frontliner with one of the best ultimate skill timings in the game — he casts 
          his AOE crowd control within the first few seconds of battle. This early cast can decide the 
          outcome of fights before they even develop. He also provides a large HP boost to the team on cast.
          Best-in-slot front line for most beginner and mid-game teams.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="hero-entry">
        <h4>Bastet <span class="tier-badge s">Top DPS / Dodge</span></h4>
        <p>
          Bastet targets high-damage enemy units and has a dodge mechanic that makes her incredibly 
          hard to punish. Every dodge she performs also deals additional damage back. 
          She is especially strong against carry-heavy enemy teams.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="hero-entry">
        <h4>Mumus <span class="tier-badge s">Support / Taunt</span></h4>
        <p>
          Mumus brings a Taunt mechanic that forces enemies to target her, protecting your key 
          damage dealers. She pairs exceptionally well with units like Bastet and Isis. 
          A great support investment that immediately improves your team's survivability.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="hero-entry">
        <h4>Hela <span class="tier-badge a">High Burst Potential</span></h4>
        <p>
          Hela is a burst damage dealer with enormous late-fight payoff. When paired with Yuelao 
          and given a few seconds to survive, she can obliterate entire enemy teams. 
          She requires some investment to reach her potential but is a worthwhile early pickup.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="hero-entry">
        <h4>Nemesis <span class="tier-badge a">Scales with Awakening</span></h4>
        <p>
          Nemesis becomes a dominant force at max relic awakening. She is a strong early-game pick 
          that keeps improving as you invest in her relic — making her a great long-term project 
          you can start immediately.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h3>🌟 Star Heroes — Who is Worth It at 1 Copy?</h3>
      <div class="team-example">
        <p>
          <strong>Good at base copy (Legendary):</strong> Nuwa, Amun Ra, Nyx, Dionysus — these provide 
          immediate value and don't require heavy investment to contribute.<br/><br/>
          <strong>Require heavy investment:</strong> Zeus, Nezha — hold off on these until you have the 
          resources to fully build them. They underperform at low investment.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h3>⚠️ Common Mistake</h3>
      <div class="warning-box">
        <p>
          Do not level multiple heroes at once. Pick 5–6 core heroes and max them before touching others. 
          A fully-built Fangi or Poseidon beats a half-built team of ten heroes every time.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- SECTION 2: RELICS -->
    <div class="content-card" id="relics">
      <h2>🔮 Relic Priority — What to Upgrade First</h2>
      <p>
        Relics are one of the biggest power multipliers in Motto Immortal. Upgrading the wrong 
        relics early is a costly mistake. Follow this priority order to maximize your efficiency.
      </p>

      <h3>Priority Tier 1 — Upgrade These First</h3>

      <div class="hero-entry">
        <h4>Fangi's Relic <span class="tier-badge sss">Highest Priority</span></h4>
        <p>
          Fangi's relic, once maxed to Level 30, transforms her into a game-defining force in PvP 
          and PvE alike. This is your first major relic investment goal. If you commit to Fangi early, 
          prioritize her relic above everything else.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="hero-entry">
        <h4>Nemesis's Relic <span class="tier-badge s">Max Awakening Target</span></h4>
        <p>
          Nemesis's power is directly tied to her relic awakening level. At max awakening she is 
          described as "insane" — meaning this relic has a very high ceiling. Invest here early 
          for a hero that keeps scaling.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h3>Priority Tier 2 — Build After Core Units</h3>

      <div class="hero-entry">
        <h4>Bastet's Relic</h4>
        <p>
          Once your Bastet is your primary DPS, upgrading her relic increases her dodge frequency 
          and damage burst. Build this after you have her fully ascended.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="hero-entry">
        <h4>Poseidon's Relic</h4>
        <p>
          Improves his crowd control potency and HP scaling. Good second tank investment.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h3>⚠️ What to Avoid</h3>
      <div class="warning-box">
        <p>
          Do not invest in Athena's relic before building your primary damage dealers. 
          Athena is a powerful support, but only reaches her full potential once you have 
          protected units worth shielding (like Bastet or Poseidon). 
          Building Athena first wastes resources that should go into your carry heroes.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="info-box">
        <p>
          <strong>💡 General Rule:</strong> Upgrade the relic of whichever hero you use in 
          the most game modes. Fangi qualifies in almost every mode — which is why she 
          consistently tops the relic priority list.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- SECTION 3: ZODIAC -->
    <div class="content-card" id="zodiac">
      <h2>♈ Zodiac Selection — Which Should Beginners Choose?</h2>
      <p>
        At the start of the game, you are asked to choose a Zodiac Sign. This is a permanent decision 
        that comes with a free Purple (Epic) hero — so choose wisely.
      </p>

      <h3>✅ Recommended Choice: Capricorn</h3>
      <div class="team-example">
        <h4>Why Capricorn?</h4>
        <p>
          Distinct Capricorn comes with a unique <strong>Hero Swap</strong> skill — the ability to 
          switch out a hero mid-combat. This provides enormous tactical flexibility, especially 
          in PvP where adapting to enemy lineups matters. Among all the Zodiac options, 
          this mechanic stands out as the most impactful for beginners who are still learning 
          the game's combat system.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h3>What Makes the Zodiac Hero Different from Other Purple Heroes?</h3>
      <p>
        Standard Epic (Purple) heroes are either offensive, defensive, or support with fixed kits. 
        The Zodiac heroes — called "Distinct" heroes — each carry a unique passive or active mechanic 
        tied to their constellation that normal Epic heroes do not have:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Distinct Cancer:</strong> Improves defensive stats of your full team</li>
        <li><strong>Distinct Gemini:</strong> Has a reliable Stun ability</li>
        <li><strong>Distinct Capricorn:</strong> Hero Swap skill — tactical mid-fight flexibility</li>
        <li><strong>Distinct Aquarius:</strong> Good utility and early-game damage</li>
        <li><strong>Distinct Virgo:</strong> Decent mid-game support in niche scenarios</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        These Distinct heroes are viable all the way through mid-game and in case-specific scenarios 
        beyond that — making your starting Zodiac pick a genuine power spike for your first few weeks.
      </p>

      <div class="info-box">
        <p>
          <strong>💡 Tip:</strong> Beginners up through mid-game can reliably use Distinct heroes 
          as a consistent team member. Don't dismiss them just because they are Epic rarity — 
          their unique mechanics punch well above their tier.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- SECTION 4: PVP NORMAL ARENA -->
    <div class="content-card" id="pvp-normal">
      <h2>🏆 PvP Team — Normal Arena</h2>
      <p>
        The Normal Arena rewards consistent team compositions over flashy mechanics. 
        Your goal is a durable, synergistic lineup that can auto-battle reliably against a wide range of enemies.
      </p>

      <h3>🎯 Best Reference Setup (Poseidon Core)</h3>
      <div class="team-example">
        <h4>Poseidon • Mumus • Bastet • Fangi • Nemesis</h4>
        <p>
          This lineup combines early crowd control (Poseidon), aggro management (Mumus), 
          high burst DPS (Bastet + Fangi), and scaling damage (Nemesis). 
          It performs reliably in both offensive and defensive arena slots.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h3>💡 Why This Lineup Works — Hero Synergy</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Poseidon</strong> opens the fight with an AOE CC that slows the enemy team — 
          giving your DPS heroes a safe window to burst.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Mumus</strong> draws enemy attention with Taunt, protecting Bastet and Fangi 
          from being focused down before they can deal damage.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Bastet</strong> capitalizes on the Mumus taunt by targeting the enemy's strongest 
          damage dealer. Her dodge keeps her alive even when she's eventually targeted.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Fangi</strong> provides cross-mode reliability. In arena specifically, 
          a Divine Fangi with Level 30 relic is a consistent carry that wins trades.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Nemesis</strong> ramps up in longer fights where the relic awakening kicks in — 
          she acts as a threat that enemies must deal with or face growing damage.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h3>📈 Suggested Lineups by Progress Stage</h3>

      <div class="stage-block beginner">
        <h4>🟢 Beginner</h4>
        <p><strong>Poseidon • Mumus • Fangi • Distinct Capricorn • Nemesis</strong></p>
        <p>
          Use your Zodiac hero (Capricorn) in the flex slot. The Hero Swap skill gives you 
          adaptability when you don't yet have a fifth strong carry. Poseidon + Mumus hold the front, 
          Fangi and Nemesis deal damage.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="stage-block midgame">
        <h4>🔵 Mid-Game</h4>
        <p><strong>Poseidon • Mumus • Bastet • Fangi • Hela</strong></p>
        <p>
          Introduce Bastet once she is properly invested. Hela joins as a late-fight cleaner — 
          when paired with Yuelao she obliterates teams. If you have Yuelao: 
          <strong>Poseidon • Mumus • Bastet • Fangi • Hela + Yuelao support</strong>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="stage-block endgame">
        <h4>🟣 End-Game</h4>
        <p><strong>Poseidon • Mumus • Bastet • Fangi • Nyx / Dionysus</strong></p>
        <p>
          At end-game, a Star Hero (Nyx or Dionysus) replaces the flex carry slot. 
          Dionysus pairs especially well with Isis if you develop an Isis team — 
          the combination of their skills with a Caishen support is one of the highest-ceiling 
          compositions in the game. Nyx is the go-to assassin carry if you pull her early.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h3>⚠️ Counter Awareness</h3>
      <div class="warning-box">
        <p>
          <strong>Anubis</strong> hard-counters mage and archer-heavy teams (low HP heroes). 
          If you face Anubis frequently in Arena, ensure you have at least one high-HP frontliner 
          absorbing hits before your squishier carries can act.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- SECTION 5: TRIPLE DUEL -->
    <div class="content-card" id="pvp-triple">
      <h2>⚡ Triple Duel — Advanced Arena Tips</h2>
      <p>
        The Triple Duel (also called "Three Kingdoms" or Advanced Arena) requires you to field 
        <strong>three separate teams</strong>. This is where depth of roster matters — 
        but there are smart ways to approach it even as a beginner.
      </p>

      <h3>📌 Core Principle: Specialization per Team</h3>
      <p>
        Each team in Triple Duel should serve a distinct role. A mixed team of mediocre heroes 
        across all three slots loses to a player who has one excellent team and two decent ones. 
        Build depth strategically.
      </p>

      <h3>🗂️ Recommended Team Distribution</h3>

      <div class="stage-block beginner">
        <h4>Team 1 — Your Best Team (Primary Carry)</h4>
        <p><strong>Poseidon • Mumus • Bastet • Fangi • Nemesis</strong></p>
        <p>Your main PvP lineup. This should be your most-invested team going into Triple Duel.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="stage-block midgame">
        <h4>Team 2 — Anti-Meta / Counter Team</h4>
        <p><strong>Anubis • [Crowd Control unit] • DPS • Support • Tank</strong></p>
        <p>
          Anubis is your secret weapon in Triple Duel. He shuts down mage and archer compositions 
          completely — when enemies run glass-cannon carries, Anubis deletes them.
          Pair him with a CC hero like Distinct Gemini (stun) or Horos (airborne immunity) 
          for maximum disruption.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="stage-block endgame">
        <h4>Team 3 — Stall / Sustain Team</h4>
        <p><strong>Aris • Prometheus • Tank • Healer • Support</strong></p>
        <p>
          Aris and Prometheus both have immunity-style stalling mechanics. This team's goal is 
          not necessarily to win, but to time-out strong enemy teams and prevent full clears. 
          Prometheus excels in PvE stall and works well in this role. Aris is particularly 
          effective in Shrine-mode and as a defensive anchor.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h3>💡 Triple Duel Tips</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Scout before assigning:</strong> Look at which enemy team is weakest and send 
          your counter team against it — don't auto-assign.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Horos counter-pick:</strong> When Horos jumps into the air, he becomes immune 
          to all damage. Position Horos on Team 2 as a surprise counter to burst-heavy lineups.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Fang is multi-mode:</strong> Fangi performs in Triple Duel just as well as in 
          Normal Arena. A Divine Fangi is the best cross-format investment you can make.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Avoid Artemis vs. Isis matchups:</strong> Artemis always loses to Isis in direct 
          confrontation. If you run Artemis, keep her away from Isis-centric enemy teams.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Panic pick: Hela + Yuelao:</strong> If you need a third team quickly and are 
          mid-game, Hela + Yuelao as a duo carry with some frontline can win fights by sheer 
          burst potential if Hela survives the opening.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <div class="info-box">
        <p>
          <strong>🎯 Long-Term Goal:</strong> Build toward having 3 distinct, fully-invested teams. 
          This is the mid-game transition point at around Week 3+. Until then, focus on your primary 
          carry team and use filler for slots 2 and 3 — you'll still earn rewards.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- PRO TIPS -->
    <div class="content-card tips-card">
      <h2>🌟 Quick Reference — Beginner Checklist</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>✅ Choose <strong>Distinct Capricorn</strong> as your starting Zodiac for the Hero Swap skill</li>
        <li>✅ Build <strong>Fangi</strong> first — she works in every game mode</li>
        <li>✅ Max <strong>Fangi's relic to Level 30</strong> as your first major relic goal</li>
        <li>✅ <strong>Poseidon + Mumus</strong> is your best early front line</li>
        <li>✅ Don't invest in Athena's relic before your carries are built</li>
        <li>✅ In Triple Duel, use <strong>Anubis</strong> to counter mage/archer teams</li>
        <li>✅ Avoid spreading upgrades across too many heroes — focus 5-6 core units first</li>
        <li>✅ Join a guild early — progression benefits are significant</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

  </main>

  <Footer />
</body>
</html>

<style>
/* RESET & BASE */
html, body {
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0;
  font-family: "Spectral", "Roboto", system-ui, sans-serif;
  background:
    radial-gradient(ellipse at 30% -10%, rgba(120,90,200,0.15), transparent 60%),
    radial-gradient(ellipse at 80% 20%, rgba(255,215,100,0.08), transparent 55%),
    linear-gradient(to bottom, #0d0b10, #07060c);
  color: #e6e6eb;
  min-height: 100vh;
}

body {
  margin-left: 48px;
}

@media (max-width: 768px) {
  body {
    margin-left: 0;
    margin-bottom: 56px;
  }
}

/* HERO SECTION */
.hero {
  position: relative;
  width: 100%;
  height: 360px;
  background-image: url("/bg.jpg");
  background-size: cover;
  background-position: center;
  background-attachment: fixed;
  display: flex;
  align-items: flex-end;
  overflow: hidden;
}

.hero-overlay {
  position: absolute;
  inset: 0;
  background: linear-gradient(
    to top,
    rgba(7, 6, 12, 0.98) 0%,
    rgba(7, 6, 12, 0.6) 50%,
    rgba(7, 6, 12, 0.2) 100%
  );
  pointer-events: none;
}

.hero-text {
  position: relative;
  z-index: 1;
  padding: 0 48px 40px;
}

.hero-tag {
  display: inline-block;
  background: rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.3);
  border: 1px solid rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.6);
  color: #c4b5fd;
  font-size: 0.75rem;
  font-weight: 600;
  letter-spacing: 0.12em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  padding: 4px 12px;
  border-radius: 20px;
  margin-bottom: 12px;
}

.hero-headline {
  margin: 0 0 8px;
  font-size: 3.5rem;
  font-weight: 700;
  color: #fff;
  text-shadow: 0 4px 20px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.8);
  line-height: 1.1;
}

.hero-sub {
  margin: 0;
  font-size: 1.1rem;
  color: rgba(230, 230, 235, 0.7);
}

@media (max-width: 768px) {
  .hero { height: 280px; }
  .hero-text { padding: 0 24px 28px; }
  .hero-headline { font-size: 2.2rem; }
}

/* MAIN CONTENT */
.main-content {
  max-width: 1000px;
  margin: 0 auto;
  padding: 48px 32px 80px;
}

/* CONTENT CARDS */
.content-card {
  background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03);
  border: 1px solid rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.3);
  border-radius: 12px;
  padding: 36px;
  margin-bottom: 32px;
  transition: border-color 0.3s ease;
}

.content-card:hover {
  border-color: rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.5);
}

.content-card h2 {
  margin-top: 0;
  margin-bottom: 20px;
  font-size: 1.9rem;
  color: #fcd34d;
  border-bottom: 2px solid rgba(250, 204, 21, 0.25);
  padding-bottom: 14px;
}

.content-card h3 {
  margin-top: 28px;
  margin-bottom: 12px;
  font-size: 1.3rem;
  color: #c4b5fd;
}

.content-card h4 {
  margin-top: 14px;
  margin-bottom: 6px;
  font-size: 1.1rem;
  color: #e6e6eb;
}

.content-card p, .content-card li {
  line-height: 1.85;
  color: #d1d1db;
  margin-bottom: 12px;
}

.content-card ul {
  margin-bottom: 16px;
  padding-left: 20px;
}

.content-card strong {
  color: #e6e6eb;
}

/* TABLE OF CONTENTS */
.toc-card {
  background: rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.06);
  border-color: rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.4);
}

.toc-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(180px, 1fr));
  gap: 12px;
  margin-top: 8px;
}

.toc-item {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 10px;
  background: rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.1);
  border: 1px solid rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.25);
  border-radius: 8px;
  padding: 12px 16px;
  color: #c4b5fd;
  text-decoration: none;
  font-size: 0.9rem;
  transition: background 0.2s, border-color 0.2s;
}

.toc-item:hover {
  background: rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.2);
  border-color: rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.5);
  color: #e9d5ff;
}

.toc-icon {
  font-size: 1.2rem;
}

/* HERO ENTRIES */
.hero-entry {
  background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03);
  border-left: 3px solid rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.5);
  border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0;
  padding: 14px 18px;
  margin: 14px 0;
}

.hero-entry h4 {
  margin: 0 0 8px;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 10px;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
}

.tier-badge {
  font-size: 0.7rem;
  font-weight: 700;
  letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  padding: 3px 9px;
  border-radius: 20px;
  vertical-align: middle;
}

.tier-badge.sss {
  background: rgba(250, 204, 21, 0.2);
  border: 1px solid rgba(250, 204, 21, 0.5);
  color: #fcd34d;
}

.tier-badge.s {
  background: rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.2);
  border: 1px solid rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.5);
  color: #c4b5fd;
}

.tier-badge.a {
  background: rgba(59, 130, 246, 0.2);
  border: 1px solid rgba(59, 130, 246, 0.4);
  color: #93c5fd;
}

/* STAGE BLOCKS */
.stage-block {
  border-radius: 8px;
  padding: 18px 20px;
  margin: 14px 0;
}

.stage-block h4 {
  margin-top: 0;
  margin-bottom: 8px;
  font-size: 1rem;
  font-weight: 700;
}

.stage-block p {
  margin-bottom: 6px;
}

.stage-block p:first-of-type {
  font-family: monospace;
  font-size: 0.95rem;
  color: #e6e6eb;
  background: rgba(0,0,0,0.2);
  padding: 6px 10px;
  border-radius: 4px;
  display: inline-block;
}

.beginner {
  background: rgba(34, 197, 94, 0.07);
  border: 1px solid rgba(34, 197, 94, 0.25);
}

.beginner h4 { color: #86efac; }

.midgame {
  background: rgba(59, 130, 246, 0.07);
  border: 1px solid rgba(59, 130, 246, 0.25);
}

.midgame h4 { color: #93c5fd; }

.endgame {
  background: rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.07);
  border: 1px solid rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.25);
}

.endgame h4 { color: #c4b5fd; }

